{"id":"mahabharata-5-105","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":105,"title":"पञ्चाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 105 · Galava's despair","summary":{"en":"Galava, unable to eat, sleep or rest, despairs of finding such horses and fears being thought ungrateful. Garuda, his friend, comes to him and offers to carry him wherever he wishes to go.","kn":"ಊಟ, ನಿದ್ರೆ, ವಿಶ್ರಾಂತಿ ಇಲ್ಲದ ಗಾಲವನು ಅಂಥ ಕುದುರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಹುಡುಕುವ ಆಸೆ ತೊರೆದು ಕೃತಘ್ನನೆನಿಸುವೆನೆಂದು ಹೆದರುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಮಿತ್ರ ಗರುಡನು ಬಂದು ಬಯಸಿದಲ್ಲಿಗೆ ಹೊತ್ತೊಯ್ಯುವೆನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"न खा पाने, न सो पाने, न विश्राम कर पाने वाले गालव ऐसे घोड़े पाने से निराश होकर कृतघ्न समझे जाने से डरते हैं। उनके मित्र गरुड़ आकर उन्हें जहाँ चाहें ले जाने का प्रस्ताव करते हैं।","te":"తిండి, నిద్ర, విశ్రాంతి లేని గాలవుడు అలాంటి గుర్రాలు దొరకవని నిరాశపడి కృతఘ్నుడనిపించుకుంటానని భయపడతాడు. మిత్రుడు గరుడుడు వచ్చి కోరిన చోటికి మోసుకువెళ్తానంటాడు.","ta":"உண்ணவும் உறங்கவும் ஓய்வெடுக்கவும் இயலாத காலவன் அத்தகைய குதிரைகளைக் கண்டுபிடிக்க முடியாது என்று நம்பிக்கை இழந்து நன்றி கெட்டவனாகக் கருதப்படுவோமோ என்று அஞ்சுகிறான். அவன் நண்பன் கருடன் வந்து விரும்பிய இடத்துக்குச் சுமந்து செல்வதாகச் சொல்கிறான்.","ml":"അത്തരം കുതിരകളെ കണ്ടെത്താനാകില്ലെന്ന് ഭയന്ന്, ഭക്ഷണവും ഉറക്കവും വിശ്രമവുമില്ലാതെ ഗാലവൻ നിരാശപ്പെടുന്നു; നന്ദികെട്ടവനെന്ന് വിചാരിക്കപ്പെടുമോ എന്നും അദ്ദേഹം ഭയക്കുന്നു. സുഹൃത്തായ ഗരുഡൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ അടുത്തെത്തി, ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നിടത്തേക്ക് കൊണ്ടുപോകാമെന്ന് വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.105; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तदा तेन विश्वामित्रेण धीमता ।\nनास्ते न शेते नाहारं कुरुते गालवस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this by the wise Vishvamitra, Galava neither sat nor slept nor took any food."}},{"n":2,"text":"त्वगस्थिभूतो हरिणश्चिन्ताशोकपरायणः ।\nशोचमानोऽतिमात्रं स दह्यमानश्च मन्युना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reduced to skin and bones, pale, given over to worry and grief, he lamented bitterly and burned with distress."}},{"n":3,"text":"कुतः पुष्टानि मित्राणि कुतोऽर्थाः संचयः कुतः ।\nहयानां चन्द्रशुभ्राणां शतान्यष्टौ कुतो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Where will I find well-nourished friends, where wealth, where savings? Where will I get eight hundred horses white as the moon?"}},{"n":4,"text":"कुतो मे भोजनश्रद्धा सुखश्रद्धा कुतश्च मे ।\nश्रद्धा मे जीवितस्यापि छिन्ना किं जीवितेन मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where is my appetite for food, where my hope of happiness? Even my hope of living is cut off. What use is life to me?"}},{"n":5,"text":"अहं पारं समुद्रस्य पृथिव्या वा परं परात् ।\nगत्वात्मानं विमुञ्चामि किं फलं जीवितेन मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall go beyond the ocean, or to the far side of the earth, and abandon myself. What is the point of my living?"}},{"n":6,"text":"अधनस्याकृतार्थस्य त्यक्तस्य विविधैः फलैः ।\nऋणं धारयमाणस्य कुतः सुखमनीहया ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one without wealth, without his purpose fulfilled, deprived of various rewards and carrying a debt, where can there be happiness without effort?"}},{"n":7,"text":"सुहृदां हि धनं भुक्त्वा कृत्वा प्रणयमीप्सितम् ।\nप्रतिकर्तुमशक्तस्य जीवितान्मरणं वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who has taken his friends' wealth and enjoyed their kind favors but cannot repay them is better dead than alive."}},{"n":8,"text":"प्रतिश्रुत्य करिष्येति कर्तव्यं तदकुर्वतः ।\nमिथ्यावचनदग्धस्य इष्टापूर्तं प्रणश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who promises, 'I shall do it,' and does not do what he must, burnt by false speech, loses the merit of his sacrifices and good works."}},{"n":9,"text":"न रूपमनृतस्यास्ति नानृतस्यास्ति संततिः ।\nनानृतस्याधिपत्यं च कुत एव गतिः शुभा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A lie has no beauty, no posterity and no lordship; how then can it have a good destination?"}},{"n":10,"text":"कुतः कृतघ्नस्य यशः कुतः स्थानं कुतः सुखम् ।\nअश्रद्धेयः कृतघ्नो हि कृतघ्ने नास्ति निष्कृतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where is fame for the ungrateful, where position, where happiness? The ungrateful cannot be trusted, and for the ungrateful there is no atonement."}},{"n":11,"text":"न जीवत्यधनः पापः कुतः पापस्य तन्त्रणम् ।\nपापो ध्रुवमवाप्नोति विनाशं नाशयन्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A sinner without wealth cannot live, so where is protection for a sinner? A sinner who ruins what was done for him surely meets destruction."}},{"n":12,"text":"सोऽहं पापः कृतघ्नश्च कृपणश्चानृतोऽपि च ।\nगुरोर्यः कृतकार्यः संस्तत्करोमि न भाषितम् ।\nसोऽहं प्राणान्विमोक्ष्यामि कृत्वा यत्नमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am that sinner, ungrateful, wretched and false, I who, having had my work done by my teacher, do not do what he has said. So I shall give up my life, after making one last supreme effort."}},{"n":13,"text":"अर्थना न मया काचित्कृतपूर्वा दिवौकसाम् ।\nमानयन्ति च मां सर्वे त्रिदशा यज्ञसंस्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have never before made a request of the dwellers of heaven, and all the gods honor me at the spread of the sacrifice."}},{"n":14,"text":"अहं तु विबुधश्रेष्ठं देवं त्रिभुवनेश्वरम् ।\nविष्णुं गच्छाम्यहं कृष्णं गतिं गतिमतां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now I shall go to the god Vishnu, best of the wise, Krishna, lord of the three worlds, goal of those who seek a goal."}},{"n":15,"text":"भोगा यस्मात्प्रतिष्ठन्ते व्याप्य सर्वान्सुरासुरान् ।\nप्रयतो द्रष्टुमिच्छामि महायोगिनमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From him all enjoyments are established, pervading all gods and Asuras. Purified, I wish to see that great yogi, the imperishable.'"}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमुक्ते सखा तस्य गरुडो विनतात्मजः ।\nदर्शयामास तं प्राह संहृष्टः प्रियकाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had spoken so, his friend Garuda, son of Vinata, appeared to him and spoke, delighted, wishing to please him."}},{"n":17,"text":"सुहृद्भवान्मम मतः सुहृदां च मतः सुहृत् ।\nईप्सितेनाभिलाषेण योक्तव्यो विभवे सति ॥","meaning":{"en":"'You are my friend, and a friend of friends, and a friend should be helped to his desire when one has the means."}},{"n":18,"text":"विभवश्चास्ति मे विप्र वासवावरजो द्विज ।\nपूर्वमुक्तस्त्वदर्थं च कृतः कामश्च तेन मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have the means, brahmin. Vishnu, Indra's younger brother, has promised me earlier on your behalf and has granted my wish."}},{"n":19,"text":"स भवानेतु गच्छाव नयिष्ये त्वां यथासुखम् ।\nदेशं पारं पृथिव्या वा गच्छ गालव माचिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So come, let us go; I shall carry you comfortably. Go to the region at the far end of the earth, Galava, without delay.'"}}]}]}